{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 1057 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "fc6525f5d06731429f3483f70babe1304d4d8bdb3d0909de4be0a87e49bc4632" :edb/db-before-t 1056 :edb/db-after-t 1057 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534369 50 #inst "2026-10-06T17:50:43.964Z" 13194139534369 true] [17592186078336 1020 #edb/ref 17592186284497 13194139534369 true] [17592186092210 1020 #edb/ref 17592186284504 13194139534369 true] [17592186100833 1020 #edb/ref 17592186284511 13194139534369 true] [17592186105639 1020 #edb/ref 17592186284490 13194139534369 true] [17592186115283 1020 #edb/ref 17592186284480 13194139534369 true] [17592186129017 1020 #edb/ref 17592186284473 13194139534369 true] [17592186129239 1020 #edb/ref 17592186284483 13194139534369 true] [17592186175847 1020 #edb/ref 17592186284466 13194139534369 true] [17592186180118 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534369 true] [17592186180118 1100 "Write $3 - \\frac{a + 2}{a - 3}$ as a single fraction." 13194139534369 false] [17592186180118 1100 "Write $3-\\frac{a+2}{a-3}$ as a single fraction." 13194139534369 true] [17592186180118 1145 "Using the fact that $3=\\frac{3}{1},$ we can write the expression as\n\n$$\n\\frac{3}{1}-\\frac{a+2}{a-3}.\n$$\n\n \n\nIn order to add the two fractions, we need them to have a common denominator. So, we put both fractions over a common denominator of $a-3$ by multiplying the top and bottom of the first fraction by $a-3:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{1}-\\frac{a+2}{a-3} & = \\\\ \\frac{a-3}{a-3}\\cdot \\frac{3}{1}-\\frac{a+2}{a-3} & = \\\\ \\frac{3(a-3)}{a-3}-\\frac{a+2}{a-3} & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we subtract the fractions and simplify the result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3(a-3)}{a-3}-\\frac{a+2}{a-3} & = \\\\ \\frac{3(a-3)-(a+2)}{a-3} & = \\\\ \\frac{3a-9-a-2}{a-3} & = \\\\ \\frac{2a-11}{a-3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534369 true] [17592186284466 1017 #edb/ref 17592186284467 13194139534369 true] [17592186284466 1089 "q-103440" 13194139534369 true] [17592186284466 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534369 true] [17592186284466 1100 "Find the equation of the line that passes through the point $(2,3)$ and is perpendicular to the line passing through the points $(1,4)$ and $(-4,6).$" 13194139534369 true] [17592186284466 1113 #uuid "8b69ae23-2c51-5627-87f4-4109cdd5f517" 13194139534369 true] [17592186284466 1145 "Perpendicular lines have slopes that are negative reciprocals of each other.\n\nFirst, let's find the slope ${m}_{1}$ of the line passing through the points $(1,4)$ and $(-4,6):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}_{1} & =\\frac{{y}_{2}-{y}_{1}}{{x}_{2}-{x}_{1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{6-4}{-4-1} \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we want a perpendicular line, the slope $m$ of the line we're trying to find must satisfy\n\n$$\nm\\cdot (-\\frac{2}{5})=-1\\,⇒\\,m=\\frac{5}{2}.\n$$\n\nWe know that the line passes through the point $(2,3).$ Using point-slope form and simplifying, we obtain the equation of the line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =m(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y-3 & =\\frac{5}{2}(x-2) \\\\ y-3 & =\\frac{5}{2}x-5 \\\\ y & =\\frac{5}{2}x-2\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534369 true] [17592186284467 1000 #edb/ref 17592186284468 13194139534369 true] [17592186284467 1000 #edb/ref 17592186284469 13194139534369 true] [17592186284467 1000 #edb/ref 17592186284470 13194139534369 true] [17592186284467 1000 #edb/ref 17592186284471 13194139534369 true] [17592186284467 1000 #edb/ref 17592186284472 13194139534369 true] [17592186284467 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534369 true] [17592186284467 1041 "selection" 13194139534369 true] [17592186284467 1104 #edb/ref 17592186284470 13194139534369 true] [17592186284467 1110 #uuid "526f0052-909b-5399-aef6-079d28911781" 13194139534369 true] [17592186284468 1034 "y=-\\frac{2}{5}x+\\frac{19}{5}" 13194139534369 true] [17592186284468 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534369 true] [17592186284468 1111 #uuid "1e985ada-2962-571b-bafe-6339b6b9c3d6" 13194139534369 true] [17592186284469 1034 "y=\\frac{1}{2}x+2" 13194139534369 true] [17592186284469 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534369 true] [17592186284469 1111 #uuid "9ad8d16d-c707-512b-8f81-bf4dd6d4f4d6" 13194139534369 true] [17592186284470 1034 "y=\\frac{5}{2}x-2" 13194139534369 true] [17592186284470 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534369 true] [17592186284470 1111 #uuid "794a7a82-8c6b-5594-a73d-0aaee8817743" 13194139534369 true] [17592186284471 1034 "y=-\\frac{5}{2}x+8" 13194139534369 true] [17592186284471 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534369 true] [17592186284471 1111 #uuid "6da59769-1bbc-5fc8-9d77-d797da84d43b" 13194139534369 true] [17592186284472 1034 "y=\\frac{2}{5}x+\\frac{11}{5}" 13194139534369 true] [17592186284472 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534369 true] [17592186284472 1111 #uuid "0ae742dc-c2af-52d4-a36d-4a2bce1b501c" 13194139534369 true] [17592186284473 1017 #edb/ref 17592186284474 13194139534369 true] [17592186284473 1089 "q-24072" 13194139534369 true] [17592186284473 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534369 true] [17592186284473 1100 "If $\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta =\\frac{2}{5}$ and $\\frac{\\pi }{2}<\\theta <\\pi $ then what is the value of $\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta ?$" 13194139534369 true] [17592186284473 1113 #uuid "ed54f9b9-6bd4-505a-bea9-8bdf8d4751e4" 13194139534369 true] [17592186284473 1145 "Let's sketch our angle $\\theta $ in the coordinate plane.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993337/assets/b81b4602d221eb04aab76b0ed8853ab75a5c3cf93e76cc489344bc15133c4daf.png)\n\nWe're given that $\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta =\\frac{2}{5}.$ We can use the Pythagorean identity to find $\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta :$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta +{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta  & =1 \\\\ {cos}^{2}⁡\\theta  & =1-{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\pm \\sqrt{1-{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta }\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta =\\frac{2}{5}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\pm \\sqrt{1-{(\\frac{2}{5})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\pm \\sqrt{1-\\frac{4}{25}} \\\\  & =\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{21}{25}} \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{21}}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe select the negative answer since $\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta $ is negative in the second quadrant. So, $\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta =-\\frac{\\sqrt{21}}{5}.$\n\nFinally, knowing that $\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta =\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta },$ we have\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta =\\frac{(\\frac{2}{5})}{(-\\frac{\\sqrt{21}}{5})}=-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{21}}=-\\frac{2\\sqrt{21}}{21}.\n$$" 13194139534369 true] [17592186284474 1000 #edb/ref 17592186284475 13194139534369 true] [17592186284474 1000 #edb/ref 17592186284476 13194139534369 true] [17592186284474 1000 #edb/ref 17592186284477 13194139534369 true] [17592186284474 1000 #edb/ref 17592186284478 13194139534369 true] [17592186284474 1000 #edb/ref 17592186284479 13194139534369 true] [17592186284474 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534369 true] [17592186284474 1041 "selection" 13194139534369 true] [17592186284474 1104 #edb/ref 17592186284477 13194139534369 true] [17592186284474 1110 #uuid "14ff7fe9-ed2b-5456-9933-6bda9b422ee2" 13194139534369 true] [17592186284475 1034 "\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta =-\\frac{2\\sqrt{21}}{63}" 13194139534369 true] [17592186284475 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534369 true] [17592186284475 1111 #uuid "1f311b5e-b5ac-5a5b-a26d-82348b2f89b3" 13194139534369 true] [17592186284476 1034 "\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta =\\frac{2\\sqrt{21}}{21}" 13194139534369 true] [17592186284476 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534369 true] [17592186284476 1111 #uuid "b0d878f1-16bf-5351-bfb2-207d5d2af168" 13194139534369 true] [17592186284477 1034 "\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta =-\\frac{2\\sqrt{21}}{21}" 13194139534369 true] [17592186284477 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534369 true] [17592186284477 1111 #uuid "dad0f8b1-1692-5294-be68-c5e70c71f41b" 13194139534369 true] [17592186284478 1034 "\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta =\\frac{3\\sqrt{21}}{105}" 13194139534369 true] [17592186284478 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534369 true] [17592186284478 1111 #uuid "c5db9fa2-c9a4-53da-9218-cb0d279103b4" 13194139534369 true] [17592186284479 1034 "\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta =\\frac{2\\sqrt{21}}{63}" 13194139534369 true] [17592186284479 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534369 true] [17592186284479 1111 #uuid "be23f83f-e7bd-551f-ba45-ec485fa67973" 13194139534369 true] [17592186284480 1017 #edb/ref 17592186284481 13194139534369 true] [17592186284480 1089 "q-263419" 13194139534369 true] [17592186284480 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534369 true] [17592186284480 1100 "What is the variance of the following data set?\n\n$$\n3,\\,18,\\,16,\\,7,\\,1,\\,12,\\,5,\\,10\n$$\n\nDo not round your answer.\n\n${\\sigma }^{2}=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139534369 true] [17592186284480 1113 #uuid "130f1ac3-a8e6-5057-ac85-84422bbb05be" 13194139534369 true] [17592186284480 1142 true 13194139534369 true] [17592186284480 1145 "If we have a data set that consists of the points ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n},$ then the variance can be computed as\n\n$$\n{\\sigma }^{2}=\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}}-(\\overset{―}{x})^{2},\n$$\n\nwhere $\\overset{―}{x}$ is the mean of the data set and $\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}}$ is the mean of the squares of the points in the data set.\n\nFirst, let's compute $\\overset{―}{x}.$ There are $n=8$ points in our data set, so the mean is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{x} & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}\\cdot (3+18+16+7+1+12+5+10) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}\\cdot 72 \\\\  & =9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's compute $\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}}.$ Computing the mean of the squares of the points in the data set, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}\\cdot ({3}^{2}+{18}^{2}+{16}^{2}+{7}^{2}+{1}^{2}+{12}^{2}+{5}^{2}+{10}^{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}\\cdot (9+324+256+49+1+144+25+100) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}\\cdot 908 \\\\  & =\\frac{908}{8} \\\\  & =\\frac{227}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the variance is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sigma }^{2} & =\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}}-(\\overset{―}{x})^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{227}{2}-{(9)}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{227}{2}-81 \\\\  & =\\frac{227-162}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{65}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534369 true] [17592186284481 1000 #edb/ref 17592186284482 13194139534369 true] [17592186284481 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534369 true] [17592186284481 1041 "field-1" 13194139534369 true] [17592186284481 1104 #edb/ref 17592186284482 13194139534369 true] [17592186284481 1110 #uuid "03b06a2f-17d0-50af-91dc-9bdb2bac7988" 13194139534369 true] [17592186284482 1034 "32.5" 13194139534369 true] [17592186284482 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534369 true] [17592186284482 1111 #uuid "f91ecf3c-df89-5000-b204-af48005278b3" 13194139534369 true] [17592186284483 1017 #edb/ref 17592186284484 13194139534369 true] [17592186284483 1017 #edb/ref 17592186284486 13194139534369 true] [17592186284483 1017 #edb/ref 17592186284488 13194139534369 true] [17592186284483 1089 "q-276683" 13194139534369 true] [17592186284483 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534369 true] [17592186284483 1100 "What is the range of the function $f(x)=\\frac{7}{2-6x}-2\\,?$\n\nThe range is\n$f(x)\\in (${{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}$)\\cup (${{field-3}}$,\\infty ).$" 13194139534369 true] [17592186284483 1113 #uuid "e3583bea-4e7e-51bc-8a8f-4cf29d2822e9" 13194139534369 true] [17592186284483 1145 "A transformed reciprocal function of the form\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{a}{bx+c}+d\n$$\n\nhas the horizontal asymptote $y=d,$ and therefore, its range is\n\n$$\nf(x)\\in (-\\infty ,d)\\cup (d,\\infty ).\n$$\n\nIn our case, $d=-2.$ Therefore, the horizontal asymptote is $y=-2,$ and the range of the function is\n\n$$\nf(x)\\in (-\\infty ,-2)\\cup (-2,\\infty ).\n$$\n\nThe graph $y=f(x)$ is shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993337/assets/27f800d93b5d4c84e98d0b7332388c5b3d513e4b896adabe6e410e4c3e3b684c.png)" 13194139534369 true] [17592186284484 1000 #edb/ref 17592186284485 13194139534369 true] [17592186284484 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534369 true] [17592186284484 1041 "field-1" 13194139534369 true] [17592186284484 1104 #edb/ref 17592186284485 13194139534369 true] [17592186284484 1110 #uuid "e5222668-bdf7-50a4-bb3a-15ec3086c2a9" 13194139534369 true] [17592186284485 1034 "-\\infty" 13194139534369 true] [17592186284485 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534369 true] [17592186284485 1111 #uuid "8373b95a-daf0-5908-ace4-1a8391cd704e" 13194139534369 true] [17592186284486 1000 #edb/ref 17592186284487 13194139534369 true] [17592186284486 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534369 true] [17592186284486 1041 "field-2" 13194139534369 true] [17592186284486 1104 #edb/ref 17592186284487 13194139534369 true] [17592186284486 1110 #uuid "abd816cc-06af-5194-89fd-a97145570daf" 13194139534369 true] [17592186284487 1034 "-2" 13194139534369 true] [17592186284487 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534369 true] [17592186284487 1111 #uuid "4ef7ad4c-cc05-5d57-814a-bd0411c3b2fb" 13194139534369 true] [17592186284488 1000 #edb/ref 17592186284489 13194139534369 true] [17592186284488 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534369 true] [17592186284488 1041 "field-3" 13194139534369 true] [17592186284488 1104 #edb/ref 17592186284489 13194139534369 true] [17592186284488 1110 #uuid "baf5396d-eafd-57c7-a859-6e88e15b7051" 13194139534369 true] [17592186284489 1034 "-2" 13194139534369 true] [17592186284489 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534369 true] [17592186284489 1111 #uuid "83efee1e-f8cc-5e07-9af8-840d0a3ed158" 13194139534369 true] [17592186284490 1017 #edb/ref 17592186284491 13194139534369 true] [17592186284490 1089 "q-29838" 13194139534369 true] [17592186284490 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534369 true] [17592186284490 1100 "Calculate $\\int \\frac{1}{x\\sqrt{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.$" 13194139534369 true] [17592186284490 1113 #uuid "74e5a7b3-a114-5a6d-a31d-10e14f2e45b8" 13194139534369 true] [17592186284490 1145 "First, we apply the constant factor rule and take the coefficient $\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{\\sqrt{2}}=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}$ out of the integral. Then we compute the integral of $\\frac{1}{x},$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{x\\sqrt{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534369 true] [17592186284491 1000 #edb/ref 17592186284492 13194139534369 true] [17592186284491 1000 #edb/ref 17592186284493 13194139534369 true] [17592186284491 1000 #edb/ref 17592186284494 13194139534369 true] [17592186284491 1000 #edb/ref 17592186284495 13194139534369 true] [17592186284491 1000 #edb/ref 17592186284496 13194139534369 true] [17592186284491 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534369 true] [17592186284491 1041 "selection" 13194139534369 true] [17592186284491 1104 #edb/ref 17592186284495 13194139534369 true] [17592186284491 1110 #uuid "bb53b84a-13f4-57c1-bd29-5e534de53b22" 13194139534369 true] [17592186284492 1034 "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(|x|+C)" 13194139534369 true] [17592186284492 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534369 true] [17592186284492 1111 #uuid "29f3f933-d6ea-5dde-99a2-93e85029be09" 13194139534369 true] [17592186284493 1034 "\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+C" 13194139534369 true] [17592186284493 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534369 true] [17592186284493 1111 #uuid "4505a44c-2f96-5e30-b699-0953a5168ef8" 13194139534369 true] [17592186284494 1034 "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\sqrt{2}|x|)+C" 13194139534369 true] [17592186284494 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534369 true] [17592186284494 1111 #uuid "73270869-4f7d-5094-9fd2-24eb93103668" 13194139534369 true] [17592186284495 1034 "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+C" 13194139534369 true] [17592186284495 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534369 true] [17592186284495 1111 #uuid "3855ff7a-93e8-5941-b04e-b8d0d9b456d9" 13194139534369 true] [17592186284496 1034 "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}|x|}{2}+C)" 13194139534369 true] [17592186284496 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534369 true] [17592186284496 1111 #uuid "54b4881f-c44f-5353-a444-ec56219f7b35" 13194139534369 true] [17592186284497 1017 #edb/ref 17592186284498 13194139534369 true] [17592186284497 1089 "q-7024" 13194139534369 true] [17592186284497 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534369 true] [17592186284497 1100 "If $f(x)=-\\frac{6}{11}x+3$, then ${f}^{-1}(x)=$" 13194139534369 true] [17592186284497 1113 #uuid "324405ab-b96b-5067-9341-26d9c7daf119" 13194139534369 true] [17592186284497 1145 "To find the inverse of a function, we follow these steps:\n\n**Step 1:** Replace $f(x)$ with $y$:\n\n$$\ny=-\\frac{6}{11}x+3\n$$\n\n**Step 2:** Swap $x$ and $y$:\n\n$$\nx=-\\frac{6}{11}y+3\n$$\n\n**Step 3:** Solve for $y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =-\\frac{6}{11}y+3 \\\\ x-3 & =-\\frac{6}{11}y \\\\ 11(x-3) & =-6y \\\\ 11x-33 & =-6y \\\\ -\\frac{11x-33}{6} & =y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 4:** Replace $y$ with ${f}^{-1}(x)$:\n\n$$\n{f}^{-1}(x)=-\\frac{11x-33}{6}\n$$" 13194139534369 true] [17592186284498 1000 #edb/ref 17592186284499 13194139534369 true] [17592186284498 1000 #edb/ref 17592186284500 13194139534369 true] [17592186284498 1000 #edb/ref 17592186284501 13194139534369 true] [17592186284498 1000 #edb/ref 17592186284502 13194139534369 true] [17592186284498 1000 #edb/ref 17592186284503 13194139534369 true] [17592186284498 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534369 true] [17592186284498 1041 "selection" 13194139534369 true] [17592186284498 1104 #edb/ref 17592186284500 13194139534369 true] [17592186284498 1110 #uuid "36d0d55f-1962-5c44-be87-c213635b0c7c" 13194139534369 true] [17592186284499 1034 "-\\frac{2x-4}{11}" 13194139534369 true] [17592186284499 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534369 true] [17592186284499 1111 